    {
        "id": "35e7927e67ce7353",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "f2167687c85f59b3",
        "name": "README — import + ISA-101 + Tier0-Edge adaptation",
        "info": "## TinyRL UNS alarm dashboard (ISA-101 style) — import notes\n\n**Requires**: palette `node-red-dashboard` and `node-red-node-ui-table` (Menu -> Manage palette -> Install) + built-in MQTT nodes.\n\n**Import**: Menu -> Import -> select file -> Deploy. Dashboard: `http://<node-red-host>:1880/ui`\nTheme note: keep the dashboard theme light/grey (Dashboard -> Theme) to match the ISA-101 baseline.\n\n**ISA-101 design rules applied**\n- Greyscale baseline: healthy states (IDLE / LEARNING / OK) are GREY; colour is reserved for abnormal\n- RED = alarm condition; YELLOW = attention/diagnostic (unlabeled 'unknown' open ask)\n- Command buttons are neutral; only LABEL is yellow (it answers an attention state)\n- Level-1 display: state banner + confidence trend + event list + command row\n- Detail data (fw, features, lib_max, node identity) intentionally left to Tier0\n\n**Broker**: default `192.168.201.99:1883` (from uns_namespace.json) — edit the\n\"UNS broker — EDIT ME\" config node.\n**Tier0-Edge**: point at your UNS broker (default `mqtt.tier0.dev:1883`) with the credentials\ngenerated on the Edge tab. Inside Tier0's built-in Node-RED, delete this broker config and\nre-select the UNS broker on each mqtt node (Tier0 binds the embedded broker by flow name).\n\n**Topics** (UNS_BASE = `v1/Plant01/Motor-Test-Area/Line1/Drive-Station-01`)\n- subscribe: `State/condition`, `State/event`, `Action/feedback` (parsed JSON)\n- publish: `Action/feedback`, QoS 1, retain=false:\n  `{\"action\":\"start\"}` | `{\"action\":\"normal\"}` | `{\"action\":\"fault\"}` |\n  `{\"action\":\"label\",\"label\":\"<slug>\",\"by\":\"human|agent|console\"}`\n\n**Cadence note**: `State/condition` is change-driven + retained (quiet = healthy), so the\n\"last update [s]\" counter is informational only — it ticks via a 5 s heartbeat inject and\ndoes NOT raise a stale alarm.\n\n**SIM injects**: editor-only, for offline testing — ignore in production.\n",
        "x": 380,
        "y": 540,
        "wires": []
    },
